 4. 📍 How cost of living affects poverty 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data : Census Bureau. Map: Erin Davis/Axios California and Louisiana have something surprising in common: Both have some of the nation's highest poverty rates when the cost of living is factored in, Axios' Russell Contreras writes from Census Bureau data. 

 The big picture: Southern states dominate America's traditional poverty rankings based on pretax income. 

 That familiar geographic divide starts to disappear when you account for more of a family's financial realities. The Supplemental Poverty Measure includes factors like taxes, work and medical expenses, and geographic differences in housing costs. Share this chart . 

 
 
