 6. 🇫🇷 France rocked by worst riots in years 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 


 A car burns in the Place de la République in Paris yesterday. Photo: Stephanie Lecocq/Reuters Police arrested at least 1,800 people across France after violent groups clashed with officers and looted shops during nationwide demonstrations that drew hundreds of thousands of people who denounced rising living costs and poor conditions in schools.

 Masked groups set fires and attacked public buildings, including city halls, in several cities. In Limoges, in central France, flames engulfed the neo-Renaissance city hall, which was built in the 19th century and survived two world wars. The building's iconic clock tower collapsed . Get the latest . 

 
 
