 7. 🗣️ Wanted: Chief small talk officers 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Illustration: Aïda Amer/Axios. Stock: Getty Images A communication-skills app is betting that a baptism by fire in small talk can help people — especially younger Americans — rebuild social confidence, Axios' Josephine Walker writes. 

 It's hiring people to approach strangers to put that theory to the test. RiseGuide is hiring Chief Small Talk Officers, recently rebranded from Head of Hanging Out to stress the seriousness of the assignment.

 The monthlong gig pays each of up to three hires $2,000, plus a budget for outings to parks, bookstores and fitness classes, where they'll strike up conversations with strangers. Share this story . 

 
 
